===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}
Via {{bor|en|la|-}}, from {{der|en|grc|πρόσθεσις||addition}}, from {{m|grc|προστίθημι||I add}}, from {{m|grc|πρός||towards}} + {{m|grc|τίθημι||I place}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*próti}}, {{m|ine-pro|*préti}} + {{m|ine-pro|*dʰédʰeh₁ti||to be putting, to be placing}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹɒsˈθiːsɪs/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-prosthesis.oga|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|prostheses}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} An artificial [[replacement]] for a body part, either internal or external.
# {{lb|en|linguistics|prosody}} [[prothesis|Prothesis]].

